      "math_academy_id": "e-4118",
      "problem": "What is the range of $y = 2(4)^x+3?$",
      "worked_solution": "The range of $4^x$ is\n\n$$\n4^x \\gt 0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $2$ and then adding $3,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{4}^{x} & >0 \\\\ 2(4)^{x} & >0 \\\\ 2(4)^{x}+3 & >0+3 \\\\ y & >3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $y \\in (3,\\infty).$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $f(x) = 2(4)^x+3$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254086/assets/ff0d83a05e89b1e56adefe7c9717232907f0f01954cb777e382349e4346776da.png)",
